---
/* The privacy policy for the Leeway apps and this site. Keep `updated` current when it changes. */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const updated = "November 3, 2026";
const contact = "support@get-leeway.com";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · Leeway"
  description="Leeway collects no personal data. Your budget stays on your device."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="container privacy">
    <p class="eyebrow">privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="privacy__date t-faint">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="panel privacy__short">
      <span class="panel__title">the short version</span>
      <p>
        Leeway collects nothing. Your budget stays on your device. There are no accounts,
        ads, analytics or tracking, and we run no server that sees your data.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      This policy covers Leeway for iPhone, the Leeway terminal app, and this website.
      "We" means the developer of Leeway.
    </p>

    <h2>Your budget</h2>
    <p>
      Both apps keep your budget (accounts, balances, plans, months, envelopes and spending)
      in a SQLite database on your device. On iPhone it sits in the app's own storage; in
      the terminal app it sits in a data folder on your computer. Neither app sends it
      anywhere, and we never see it.
    </p>
    <p>
      On iPhone, the database is part of your device backups if you back up to iCloud or
      a computer. Apple handles those backups under its own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. The apps have no analytics, advertising or tracking code, and they don't ask
      for your name, email address, location, contacts or any other personal data.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you turn on "Share with App Developers" in your iPhone's settings, Apple may send
      us crash reports and basic usage figures. Apple strips these of anything that
      identifies you before we see them. We use them only to fix bugs.
    </p>

    <h2>Leeway Pro</h2>
    <p>
      Leeway Pro is an optional one-time purchase planned for the iPhone app. It hasn't
      shipped yet. When it does, its features will handle your data like this:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Purchase.</strong> Apple processes the payment. We learn only that the
        purchase was made, never your name or payment details.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>iCloud sync.</strong> Your budget syncs through your own private iCloud
        database. Amounts, payees and labels are encrypted end to end, so neither Apple nor
        we can read them. It counts against your iCloud storage, not ours.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sharing.</strong> If you share a budget with a partner, iCloud sends the
        invite and stores the shared copy. Either of you can stop sharing at any time.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Bank sync.</strong> If you link your bank through
        <a href="https://www.simplefin.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SimpleFIN Bridge</a>,
        the app fetches balances and transactions from SimpleFIN straight to your phone.
        Leeway never sees your bank password. The app keeps the SimpleFIN access key in your
        device's Keychain. SimpleFIN's own privacy policy covers the data it holds.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a set of static pages. It sets no cookies and runs no analytics.
      Cloudflare hosts it and Google Fonts serves its fonts; both receive your IP address
      and browser details when you load a page, as any web host does, and handle them under
      their own privacy policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      Delete the iPhone app, or the terminal app's data folder, and your budget is gone. If
      you used iCloud sync, you can also remove Leeway's iCloud data under Settings → your
      name → iCloud → Manage Account Storage.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Leeway is not meant for children under 13 and collects no data from anyone.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, we'll post the new version here and update the date at the
      top.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy { max-width: 760px; padding-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 56px; }
  .privacy h1 { font-size: clamp(28px, 4.5vw, 44px); margin-top: 12px; }
  .privacy__date { margin: 10px 0 36px; font-size: 13px; }
  .privacy__short { margin-bottom: 36px; padding: 28px 26px 22px; }
  .privacy__short p { margin: 0; color: var(--text); }
  .privacy h2 { font-size: 18px; margin: 40px 0 12px; color: var(--mauve); }
  .privacy p, .privacy li { color: var(--dim); }
  .privacy strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .privacy ul { padding-left: 1.2em; }
  .privacy li { margin-bottom: 12px; }
</style>
